cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "INHERIT — Open Estate Data Interchange Standard"
message: "If you use INHERIT in your research or software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: standard
authors:
  - name: "Testate Technologies Ltd"
    website: "https://www.openinherit.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/openinherit/standard"
url: "https://www.openinherit.org"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-04-04"
keywords:
  - estate-planning
  - open-standard
  - json-schema
  - probate
  - wills
  - trusts
  - succession
  - legal-tech
abstract: >-
  INHERIT is an open data standard for estate planning information.
  It provides a common JSON format for representing people, assets,
  liabilities, bequests, trusts, executors, and all the other entities
  that make up an estate plan — across common law, civil law, Islamic,
  Jewish, Hindu, Japanese, and African customary legal traditions.
